Title: Recognise AmigaDOS absolute paths (Volume:...)
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: std::filesystem::path::is_absolute() is false for AmigaDOS paths such as "RAM Disk:w/ls/data/x.js", so the scripting code joined them to the current directory ("AROS:/RAM Disk:w/...") and the script file formats (C array, PPM) never loaded; the file selector location bar and the launcher had the same check.
Change: base::is_absolute_path(): the std::filesystem rule, plus on AROS a volume or assign name before the first slash. Used in app_scripting.cpp (2), filesystem_script.cpp, tools_script.cpp, file_selector.cpp and launcher.cpp.
Scope: all platforms (AROS rule only under __AROS__)
Upstream: candidate
Verification: mainline x86_64, pool v1-1, 2026-11-16: log shows "Reading file RAM Disk:w/ls/data/scripts/formats/c_array.js" and ppm.js with no "Could not open"; before: "Could not open AROS:/RAM Disk:w/...". Same message seen before the fix on ABIv11 and the Pi.
Removal: when upstream handles AmigaDOS paths.
